a file diff. The rails: (1) an op on the update owner, would-restart? TREE, answered by the same restart-for over runtime-for that landed! asks, so a session or a land asks the system before it lands, never a diff of its own; bin/land prints its answer before main moves. (2) :seon.config.build/inputs is a build input of itself: a change to the list is a restart, and restart-for says so by name. Proof, red first: seon.source-test/a-change-to-the-input-list-is-a-restart. ONE WRITER OF THE MERGES TREE (root, 2026-11-15 22:2x [deps M]): 9559445556's update FAILED, bin/update's merge into .worktrees/merges hit index.lock racing another git writer of that worktree (the write-back's, likely). Two writers of one index is this owner's job: the :git effect becomes the ONE writer of the merges tree, the write-back's commits and the update's merge alike, as messages to it in order; ranked first in the update owner's next slice (slice 2), beside update/await-update. Proof, red first: an update's merge and a write-back sent at once both land, in order, with no index.lock. SLICE 2a PLAN, THE MERGES TREE'S ONE WRITER (runtime, 2026-11-15 23:4x, for flow's review before code). PRIOR WORK, read: the tree's two writers are (1) the :git effect, seon.fx/git-commit (fx.clj:788), declared {:workers 1} (resources/seon/system.edn:69), which commits a checked-out branch through its tree (commit-in-tree!, fx.clj:770) and is asked by my.root/write-back! (root.clj:187) and the reconciler's write-back (reconcile.clj:1329); (2) bin/update's merges_catch_up (bin/update:31-41), shell git in the same worktree: update-index --refresh, a clean check, merge --no-edit main, an ancestor check. The race (deps' M, 9559445556's index.lock) is (2) beside (1). CHANGE: the merge becomes a request of the same effect: seon.fx/git-commit takes {:merge ref} (beside :files), and merges ref into the checked-out tree with the same steps, through the tree, refused typed (:seon.fx/io-error naming the tree's own change)